#: desc: Without a Makefile and with an empty stdin, the help is printed (the awk args line below is intentionally empty)

#: stdout
Usage: awk [-v option=value] -f makefile-doc.awk [Makefile ...] (default: stdin)
Description: Generate docs for Makefile variables and targets
Version: @VERSION@
Options (current values):
  VARS              show documented variables (0 or 1)   "1"
  DEPRECATED        show deprecated anchors (0 or 1)     "1"
  PADDING           character between anchors and docs   " "
  OFFSET            spaces after the longest name        "3"
  WARN              print warnings on stderr (0 or 1)    "1"
  COLOR             use colors (0 or 1)                  "1"
  OUTPUT_FORMAT     ANSI, HTML or LATEX                  "ANSI"
  EXPORT_THEME      colors of the HTML and LaTeX output  ""
  SUB               rename anchors and list values       ""
  DSUB              replace text in docs and names       ""
  RECIPEPREFIX      the .RECIPEPREFIX of the Makefile    "\t"
  COLOR_DEFAULT     anchors documented with ##           "34"
  COLOR_ATTENTION   anchors documented with ##!          "31"
  COLOR_DEPRECATED  anchors documented with ##%          "33"
  COLOR_SECTION     sections                             "32"
  COLOR_BACKTICKS   text in backticks                    "33"
#: exit: 1
